.TH CUTTING-GARDEN-RESTORE 1
.SH NAME
cutting-garden-restore - restore a captured tree from a receipt blob
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B receipt-id
markl-id of the capture receipt blob to materialize.
.TP
.B dest
destination directory. MUST NOT exist; restore creates it. Restored entries land under <dest>/<root>/ per the receipt's root keys (see FDR 0001 §Behavior).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/madder/<store>/
default blob-store-id resolution root. Receipt and entry blobs are fetched from here unless -store overrides.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Capture a tree and restore it into a fresh directory.
.B rid=$(cutting-garden capture -format json src | jq -r '.id') && cutting-garden restore "$rid" out
.TP
Override the receipt's store-hint when the local store has been re-configured since capture.
.B cutting-garden restore -store .work <receipt-id> out
.SH SEE ALSO
cutting-garden(1), cutting-garden-capture(1), cutting-garden-diff(1)
